se after a natural disaster?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Names like Storm, Tempest, and Avalanche are powerful and widely used in the horse world. Avoid names associated with specific disasters that caused significant loss of life. The line between powerful and inappropriate is usually clear — if the name makes people think of tragedy rather than nature's beauty, choose differently.\"}]]}]\n2f:[\"$\",\"details\",\"7\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Should nature names match my horse's breed origin?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"It is a lovely bonus when they align — an Icelandic horse named Glacier or a Mustang named Sierra — but absolutely not a requirement. A Thoroughbred named Denali or a Warmblood named River works beautifully regardless of breed origin.\"}]]}]\n30:[\"$\",\"details\",\"8\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Are two-word nature names acceptable for registered horses?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Many breed registries allow or even encourage two-word names, and nature themes are among the most popular for registered names. Combinations like Mountain Storm, River Dance, or Desert Wind create beautiful, distinctive registered names that honor both nature and your horse's individual character.\"}]]}]\n31:[\"$\",\"details\",\"9\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"How do I test if a nature name suits my horse?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"m